    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "p2-assessor-v6",
  "source_purpose_mask": [
    "external_evidence",
    "model_output"
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s0",
      "source_id": "61c47e8d-9157-4de5-94ce-b1bad7333b3c",
      "text": "Funny how a bird and a missing sock can make everything feel both messy and just right. I’ll take that kind of surprise over perfect plans any day. Grounding? Maybe. Peace? Hopefully. Anyway, thanks for listening—even the little things feel lighter after talking. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s1",
      "source_id": "214011c6-005f-4a3f-8fef-524a26bbe6b5",
      "text": "\"It sounds like the world is full of these tiny, unexpected moments—the kind that make everything feel both chaotic and perfectly fine at the same time.\""
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s2",
      "source_id": "d6b7d92b-d73c-4c0a-9e5e-0cc02e939530",
      "text": "Yeah, exactly—like the universe winks at you between power outages and misplaced mittens. I was digging through the shed this morning, half-convinced I’d find a working lantern, and instead found last summer’s jar of honey, forgotten and crystallized. Still good, though. Kind of sweet, in a stubborn way. Makes you think maybe chaos isn’t the opposite of order—just its weird cousin."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s3",
      "source_id": "91eea1a0-b5af-4c8c-ad7b-e5c63be3520b",
      "text": "\"That sounds like finding a little unexpected treasure—a sweet, crystallized surprise in the midst of your everyday life. Sometimes the most unexpected moments, even the messy ones, are the most 'sweet' parts. I hope that 'sweet, in a stubborn way' feels like a small moment of unexpected magic in your day.\""
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "938f2bd9-4866-4a65-ac62-8b25bc8f5acf",
      "text": "It really was—like the shed decided to remind me it’s not all tangled wires and expired batteries. That jar’s been sitting there since August, quietly doing its own thing, and still ended up exactly what I needed this morning with my tea. Makes you wonder what else is hiding in plain sight, just waiting for the right moment to be useful. Or delicious. Or both."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "5e58b638-daa0-4520-b19d-dfada50fb99b",
      "text": "\"It sounds like the world is full of these tiny, unexpected treasures—moments like those in the shed, waiting patiently, only to be useful when they are needed. There is a quiet, persistent kind of magic in the way things happen, even when they are buried deep inside the ordinary.\""
    }
  ]
}

